<section class="reference-section" id="krishna-sudama"><div class="reference-section-heading"><h2>Krishna and Sudama · A Friendship Beyond Wealth</h2><a href="/krishna-sudama.html">Return to story</a></div><div class="reference-content"><p><strong>Srimad Bhagavata Purana · Skandha 10 · chapters 80–81.</strong> This original condensed English retelling follows the owner-supplied Gita Press Sanskrit–Hindi <em>Srimad Bhagavat Mahapuran</em>, Volume 2 (Skandhas 9–12). The private source PDF is not copied into the public website.</p><div class="source-list"><a href="https://archive.org/details/srimad-bhagavat-mahapuran-2-volume-set-sanskrit-hindi/Srimad%20Bhagavat%20Mahapuran%20Volume%202%20Sanskrit%20Hindi/mode/2up" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span>Read the supplied second volume</span><small>Internet Archive · Gita Press · Sanskrit with Hindi explanation</small></a></div><ol><li><strong>10.80.5–15 · private PDF pp. 919–921</strong><small>Sudama’s household, his wife’s appeal, four handfuls of flattened rice and the journey to Dvaraka.</small></li><li><strong>10.80.16–27 · private PDF pp. 921–923</strong><small>Entry into Krishna’s palace, Krishna’s embrace, the washing of Sudama’s feet, Rukmini’s service and the household’s astonishment.</small></li><li><strong>10.80.28–45 · private PDF pp. 923–926</strong><small>The friends remember Sandipani’s gurukula, their night gathering fuel in the storm and their teacher’s blessing.</small></li><li><strong>10.81.1–11 · private PDF pp. 927–928</strong><small>Krishna asks about the gift, finds the flattened rice, receives one handful and is stayed by Rukmini.</small></li><li><strong>10.81.12–23 · private PDF pp. 929–930</strong><small>Sudama’s night in the palace, his departure without asking for wealth and his meditation on Krishna’s welcome.</small></li><li><strong>10.81.24–41 · private PDF pp. 931–933</strong><small>The transformed household, abundance received without attachment, Sudama’s wish for loving friendship and the narrative’s concluding liberation.</small></li></ol><p><strong>Editorial boundary.</strong> The journey, welcome, gurukula memory, gift, Rukmini’s intervention and transformed household belong to the source narrative. The reflection on friendship beyond status is editorial. This page does not present the episode as a transactional promise of wealth.</p><p>All three images are newly AI-generated devotional interpretations. The Dvaraka palace, gurukula landscape, clothing and faces are imagined rather than historical reconstructions. The card still life contains no manuscript text and is symbolic.</p><a href="/mahapuranas.html#bhagavata">Meet the Bhagavata Purana</a></div></section>
